15 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Schematic illustration contains two sections: A shows an experimental timeline with SD rats, steps from acclimation to induction, confirmation, drug administration, and tissue analysis using histology, immunofluorescence, western blot, flow cytometry, and ELISA; B proposes Tuoli Tuonong Decoction mechanism in granulomatous lobular mastitis, showing shifts from lesion inflammation and pyroptosis to caspase-8-mediated death-mode reprogramming and tissue repair.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays close-up photographs of mammary lesions in experimental groups labeled as Control, Model, TF, TO, TTN, MP, and C8i, showing differing severity and lesion characteristics. Panel B presents a line graph comparing changes in body weight of GLM rats during treatment, with multiple colored lines representing each group across a twenty-five day timeline. Panel C shows a line graph of mammary lesion length over the same period, with separate lines for each group, indicating reductions or stability in lesion size throughout treatment.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Panel of microscopic images showing stained mammary tissue sections at varying magnifications \(40X or 400X/200X\) using H&E, Oil Red O, and Masson's trichrome across seven experimental groups: Control, Model, TF, TO, TTN, MP, and C8i. Each stain panel highlights tissue morphology, lipid accumulation, or collagen content, with specific regions enlarged to illustrate histological differences among groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows TUNEL assay immunofluorescence images \(DAPI, TUNEL, merge\) of mammary tissues across seven groups, with an adjacent bar graph comparing apoptosis levels. Panel B displays GSDMD, F4/80, and CD11c immunofluorescence staining in macrophage subsets, with merged images, and three bar graphs demonstrating expression levels in each group. Panel C presents p-MLKL, F4/80, CD11c immunofluorescence and merged images for the same groups, accompanied by bar graphs quantifying marker intensities. Panel D includes transmission electron microscopy images of macrophages in mammary tissues at 12,000X and 20,000X magnifications, illustrating cellular ultrastructure differences among groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Figure with five experimental panels labeled A through E shows qPCR, Western blot, and quantification bar graphs analyzing cell death pathways. Panels cover caspase-8, apoptosis, pyroptosis, and necroptosis in different treatment groups, with statistical significance indicated on bar graphs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
